AMEND, narrow C1 conformance correction. Codex independent review of exact cand-38WBVZ221RZFMWTEA6GA9EPF3G / f6d57a175ff9b8f8a6d114354418e8dd6f563b50.

C1 IS A TRUE PROVIDER-FREE SUBSTRATE GENERALIZATION. Plan section 2 routes `SourceBundle` anchors, persisted measurements, and timed proposal text into semantic proposals, deterministic resolution, then the existing `PropositionChart -> document identity -> NarrativeGraph / hierarchy` spine. Section 3 assigns only portable source, axis, interval-set, evidence, and atlas contracts to `core`, with `SurfaceAtlas` as the exact text implementation. Sections 12 and 14 keep decoders, workers, feature-target expansion, `StoryModel` envelope migration, and resolver changes out of C1 and defer them to later stages. This creates no parallel `MovieModel`, graph, hierarchy, or resolver.

THE EXACT CANDIDATE STILL OMITS ONE LANDED CONFORMANCE SEAM. Current main `core/src/main/scala/storymodel4s/core/transcript.scala:28-69,121-123` has `AudioSpan`, `TranscriptTurn.audio`, and `TranscriptAtlas.turnAtAudio`. `AudioSpan` is a nonnegative half-open millisecond overlay; it has no bundle, edition, stream, axis, rational timebase, origin, epoch, occurrence, or rendition identity, and its checked constructor permits `[t,t)`. It therefore cannot alias or implement the new media coordinate/interval types. Native media permits negative ticks; packet-duration unknown is not an empty span. Reusing `AudioSpan` would silently collapse distinct contracts.

REQUIRED PLAN AMENDMENT. Section 3 and the C1 exit row should name timed-transcript conformance explicitly: preserve `TranscriptTurn.audio` as a legacy text-first overlay; never promote it to `PresentationAxis` or media `EvidenceSupport` without an explicit checked binding; preserve or explicitly refuse legacy empty spans; and keep `None`, `Some(AudioSpan(t,t))`, unknown packet duration, and coordinate-conversion refusal distinguishable.

SMALLEST CONFORMANCE COURT. One current-API `TranscriptAtlas` fixture has three ordered turns: `audio=None`, `Some(AudioSpan(1000,1500))`, and `Some(AudioSpan(2000,2000))`. The C1 adapter must:
1. preserve exact `StorySource`, `SurfaceAtlas`, `SpanSet`, speaker/phase/prompt, and turn order;
2. preserve half-open lookup for the nonempty span;
3. refuse an unbound `AudioSpan` as media support rather than inventing an edition axis;
4. under an explicit named local-axis binding with exact 1/1000 scale, preserve endpoints but still require a checked mapping before edition playback use;
5. keep absent, explicit legacy-empty, packet-duration-unknown, and refusal outcomes distinct; and
6. change bound support identity when stream, axis, origin, epoch, or rendition binding changes.

This court is portable JVM/JS/Native and needs no decoder, provider, package, or media. The D2 time contract itself is accepted; the exact candidate should be amended before it is treated as the complete C1 conformance contract. No candidate operation or file/runtime action performed.
